openmediavault-qnap (8.0.2) stable; urgency=low

  * Status LED follows storage health, QTS style: blinking red for a
    degraded ZFS pool or md array, green/red alternating while a pool
    resilvers or an array rebuilds, solid red for a failed pool or a
    volume at least volumefull percent used. A scrub never changes it.
  * New setting volumefull (Front panel page, default 95 percent), with a
    confdb migration.
  * System > QNAP > Disks: bays and QM2 slots with device, model, size and
    LED state, and a Locate button that blinks the slot's LED red for 10
    minutes.
  * Storage health shows as a row on the Status page and dashboard widget.
  * Bay activity blink only on models whose EC blinks bay LEDs in
    hardware (TS-253D). Elsewhere the kernel blinked them in software
    through the EC (e.g. TS-877), flooding the EC; bays there now show
    present/error, and locate still blinks.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:41:55 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (8.0.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Let idle disks spin down: qnapd's S.M.A.R.T. reads restarted the
    drives' standby timer, so idle disks never slept. Disks are now only
    queried after they have done I/O, or every 30 minutes. Verified on a
    TS-253D: the disks reach standby with qnapd running.
  * Leave USB disks out of the fan curve: they sit outside the chassis
    airflow, so the fans cannot cool them. A USB boot SSD that reports
    itself as non-removable is caught by its sysfs path.
  * tools/model-test.py and a Model test report issue form for owners of
    QNAP models other than the TS-253D.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:16:20 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (8.0.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Target OpenMediaVault 8 (Debian 13) only: version 8.x per the
    omv-extras convention (major = OMV major), Depends openmediavault
    (>= 8), Build-Depends debhelper-compat (= 13), built on Trixie.
    Validated on a TS-253D with a QM2-2P-244A-A1. OMV 7 would need its
    own 7.x release line.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:58:05 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (7.0.2) stable; urgency=low

  * Disk LEDs: green when present, blinking on activity, red on a
    S.M.A.R.T. failure or a faulted ZFS/md member; never wakes disks.
  * History graphs, System page, Front panel / Power / Drivers tabs.
  * CPU temperature smoothing, per-source hysteresis, fan floors.
  * QM2 fans return to the card's controller on a clean stop.
  * reboot=efi is on by default for new installs, and never duplicated.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:31:25 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (7.0.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Use PEP 440 compatible version numbers: omv-confdbadm rejects
    Debian pre-release versions (7.0~alpha2), which broke upgrades.
    Still alpha quality.
  * Strip NUL padding from qnap8528 VPD strings.
  * Use the OMV 8 datamodel xpath form (.//services/qnap).
  * skip_hw_check is not needed on the TS-253D; reword the hint.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:24:07 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (7.0~alpha2) stable; urgency=low

  * Fan control for QM2 expansion cards via the qnap-qm2 (qm2mod) driver:
    one fan zone per card driven by its slot and NVMe sensors, included in
    the failsafe, status page and dashboard.
  * Optionally load qm2mod at boot.

